<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The plague's tell. Modelled on vanilla's Fleck_ToxGasSmall, which is the shape
    every atmospheric cloud in this game has: a gas texture rather than a smoke
    puff, alpha in the sixties rather than opaque, growing as it drifts up-map, and
    gone inside a second. Smoke is the wrong def for this - it is solid for six
    seconds and fades for another three, so a tint on it leaves hard coloured decals
    lying about the map instead of a haze passing over it.

    The colour lives here and not in FleckCreationData.instanceColor because alpha
    is the whole point: a fleck's instanceColor is combined with a separately
    computed fade alpha, while graphicData's is baked into the material and stays
    put. Dusty rose, not magenta - it has to read against grass and dirt without
    becoming the brightest thing on screen.
  -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="FleckBase_Thrown">
    <defName>SlopPlagueGas</defName>
    <altitudeLayer>MoteOverhead</altitudeLayer>
    <fadeInTime>0.3</fadeInTime>
    <solidTime>0</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>1.8</fadeOutTime>
    <growthRate>0.8</growthRate>
    <acceleration>(0, 0, 2)</acceleration>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Gas/GasCloudThickA</texPath>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
      <color>(214, 92, 168, 64)</color>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

  <!--
    The cat's tell, and deliberately the same cloud in the other colour: same
    texture, same alpha, same drift up-map, so the two read as one weather with
    two directions rather than as a haze and an unrelated sparkle. A cleaning
    mote would have been the obvious pick and is the wrong one - it says a chore
    was done, where this has to say the same thing the pink says, which is that
    something is happening to this ground.

    Pale green, and paler than the plague is pink: the aura is a handful of cells
    against a circle that eats the map, and it should read as the map breathing
    rather than as the brightest thing on it.
  -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="FleckBase_Thrown">
    <defName>SlopCleanAir</defName>
    <altitudeLayer>MoteOverhead</altitudeLayer>
    <fadeInTime>0.3</fadeInTime>
    <solidTime>0</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>1.8</fadeOutTime>
    <growthRate>0.8</growthRate>
    <acceleration>(0, 0, 2)</acceleration>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Gas/GasCloudThickA</texPath>
      <shaderType>TransparentPostLight</shaderType>
      <color>(148, 226, 160, 52)</color>
    </graphicData>
  </FleckDef>

</Defs>
